<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
<OpenGeoSysProject>
<!--
  DSM micro-macro potential-exchange benchmark: parameter and calibration
  provenance.

  This configuration is a plumbing/smoke test of the micro-macro potential
  exchange coupling in RichardsMechanics, not a physically calibrated
  benchmark. Several material parameters below are uncited working values,
  used to exercise the coupling numerically rather than to reproduce a
  measured material response; each is flagged as an uncited working value
  in the list below. Where a literature or specification source could be
  identified for a quantity, it is cited.

  Geometry lineage: BEACON. No BEACON specification document with a
  citable locator has been identified for this configuration; the
  parameter set below is therefore not attributed to a specific BEACON
  deliverable.

  Geometry / BC    : axisymmetric cell on beacon_1b_domain.vtu, p_ic =
                     -1e6 Pa, top_pressure 0 Pa and bottom_pressure 1e4 Pa
                     (through-flow drive), t_end = 1e3 s.
  Purpose          : micro-macro exchange plumbing smoke test, softer and
                     more permeable variant of 1a01 (E = 40e6 Pa, phi0 =
                     0.5, k = 5e-16 m2). Potential-exchange (Pi) path
                     inactive (K absent, vdW off).

  Calibration anchor:
    source         : none. This deck performs no calibration.
    dataset row    : n/a
    target sigma   : n/a
    fitted K       : none. No potential_augmentation_prefactor tag is
                     present, so K defaults to 0.0 and the augmentation
                     branch is skipped (PotentialExchange.h:259, "Setting
                     K = 0 (default) reduces exactly to the pure vdW
                     form"). The Dixon/Villar calibration-anchor
                     requirement therefore does not apply here; it is not
                     violated. The swelling_pressures literals below are
                     inputs to the macro SaturationDependentSwelling law;
                     they are NOT calibration targets and must not be
                     read as an anchor row.

  Material parameters (source per group):
    elastic nu (0.2)           : documented, family not settled. D3.3 PDF
                                 p.66, Table 2 "Mechanical parameters", row
                                 "Poisson's Ratio" = 0.2 (-). Matches this
                                 deck's live value exactly; this entry
                                 documents the literal already present and
                                 changes nothing. Source: BEACON Deliverable
                                 D3.3, "Description of the constitutive models
                                 developed in the project. Conceptual bases,
                                 mathematical description and model
                                 capabilities. Assessment of predictive
                                 power"; its title page reads "Author: Antonio
                                 Gens", with contributions by V. Kumar (this
                                 repo's owner), S. Beese, D. Masin and others;
                                 Euratom research and training programme
                                 2014-2018, grant agreement No 745 942;
                                 deliverable dated 31/10/21. Table 2 sits in
                                 the annex whose footer reads "D3.3 - BGR
                                 Results of Task 3.3", dissemination level PU,
                                 date of issue 08/09/2021. Relayed, not
                                 originated: the same page states that the
                                 mechanical parameters used in the simulations
                                 of the two stress paths are based on values
                                 stated in Akesson et al. 2010, so D3.3 Table
                                 2 restates nu rather than originating it, and
                                 that sentence's scope is D3.3's own two
                                 stress paths, not this deck. D3.3's own
                                 reference list, PDF p.72, identifies that
                                 citation as SKB TR-10-44, "SR-Site Data
                                 report. THM modelling of buffer, backfill and
                                 other system component", Akesson, Borgesson
                                 and Kristensson 2010 (names written ASCII
                                 here; the source spells them with Nordic
                                 diacritics). The TR-10-44 PDF itself is not
                                 on this machine, but a full text extraction
                                 of it is: eurad-anchors subtask41, audits,
                                 folder
                                 2026-09-03_E_vs_rhod_search_successful,
                                 lane4/txt, file
                                 SKB_SRSite_data_Akesson2010.txt. That file's
                                 own title page and running headers read
                                 "SR-Site Data report - THM modelling of
                                 buffer, backfill and other system
                                 components", "TR-10-44", "ISSN 1404-0344",
                                 authors Akesson, Borgesson, Kristensson,
                                 March 2010 - matching D3.3's reference-list
                                 entry exactly. Its Section 12.1 "Code_Bright
                                 data for MX-80", Table 12-1 "Data used for
                                 different MX-80 buffer materials
                                 (Code_Bright)" (compacted bentonite buffer:
                                 ring/block/pellets, not backfill), spanning
                                 the report's own pp. 80-81, carries Poisson's
                                 ratio 0.2, listed once across the ring, block
                                 and pellet columns. Do not confuse this file
                                 with its neighbour in the same folder,
                                 SKB_TR-10-11_Akesson2010.txt: that is a
                                 DIFFERENT SKB report (TR-10-11, "THM
                                 modelling of buffer, backfill and other
                                 system components - Critical processes and
                                 scenarios", Akesson, Kristensson, Borgesson,
                                 Dueck and Hernelind); an earlier version of
                                 this header cited that report's Tab. 7-1 /
                                 Tab. 16-3 (both backfill-material rows) for
                                 this citation, which was wrong on two counts
                                 at once: wrong report and wrong material.
                                 D3.3 does not name which TR-10-44 table it
                                 drew on, so the exact upstream row stays
                                 unestablished. Family: 12.1 family 1 (Beacon)
                                 is the candidate, not a settled
                                 classification. Family 1 reads "Beacon
                                 project benchmark spec / Beacon experimental
                                 reports", while D3.3 is a constitutive model
                                 description deliverable reporting parameters
                                 used in a simulation. That call is Vinay's.
    elastic E (40e6 Pa)        : uncited working value (E = 40e6 Pa);
                                 unchanged by this entry and still uncited.
                                 This stiffness is unique to this deck within
                                 the RichardsMechanics benchmark set. D3.3
                                 Table 2 cited above gives E = 180 MPa, which
                                 is NOT this deck's value and therefore does
                                 not document it.
    porosity split phi0/phi_tr : uncited working values (0.5 / 0.4).
    intrinsic permeability     : uncited working value (5e-16 m2).
    retention macro (Sr,m,p_b) : uncited working values (0.0 / 0.5 /
                                 5e5 Pa).
    retention micro (Sr,m,p_b) : uncited working values (0 / 0.5 /
                                 5e6 Pa).
    swelling law (p_sw, expts) : uncited working values (1.1e7 Pa x3,
                                 1 1 1).
    solid density rho_s        : uncited working value (2780 kg/m3). The
                                 "EURAD-2 MS33 spec" attribution used for
                                 this quantity in the sibling MS33
                                 headers does not apply here: the
                                 referenced Table TH-G does not contain a
                                 solid density value; the figure appears
                                 only in the EURAD-2 MS33 task
                                 specification prose
                                 ("theoretical_benchmarking", around line
                                 102) as 2.78 g/cm3, not in the table.
                                 Note also that this deck sets
                                 micro_solid_density_reference = 2650
                                 alongside solid density 2780, i.e. two
                                 grain densities about 4.7 percent apart
                                 in one file.
    micro reference state      : uncited working values (rho_SR_m =
                                 2650 kg/m3, nS_ref, n_l0). Note: 2650
                                 kg/m3 coincides with the grain density
                                 of Boom Clay reported in GRS-202; that
                                 source refers to a different material
                                 and does not apply here.
    fluid properties           : uncited working values (viscosity
                                 1e-3 Pa s, density 1e3 kg/m3). These are
                                 rounded values, not the IAPWS-95 figures
                                 at 293.15 K (1.002e-3 Pa s, 998.21
                                 kg/m3), so an IAPWS locator does not
                                 cover them.
    biot_coefficient           : uncited working value (1.0), used here
                                 as an incompressible-mineral-phase
                                 assumption rather than a measured
                                 quantity.
    mass transfer alpha_M      : uncited working value (1e-13);
                                 phenomenological and fabric-dependent,
                                 not identified via swelling-pressure
                                 calibration (fast-exchange limit).
    reference temperature      : uncited working value (293.15 K); inert
                                 in this isothermal configuration.
    BC / IC magnitudes         : uncited working values. The suction
                                 initial conditions, hydraulic Dirichlet
                                 values, sigma0 (zero) and the zero body
                                 force are not attributed to a source.
                                 For reference, the EURAD-2 MS33 task
                                 specification's initial suction is
                                 100 MPa, two orders of magnitude (100x)
                                 above the values used here, so the MS33
                                 value cannot be inherited directly.
    macro_porosity_floor and
    micro_water_content_floor  : 0.0 / 0.0, numerical and inert. Both
                                 keys must be declared together for the
                                 parser to accept the block; a floor of 0
                                 is byte-identical to the unfloored code
                                 path (PotentialExchange.h:199-205).
    micro EOS (a, b, rho_l0)   : uncited working values.
    vdW base A_Hamaker         : numerical placeholder, with the van der
                                 Waals augmentation term switched off.
                                 A = 1e-30 J, paired with
                                 specific_surface = 1.0, reduces the
                                 prefactor A*Sa^3/(6*pi) to about 1e-19
                                 of its physical magnitude. An exact zero
                                 is rejected by a positivity guard in the
                                 parser (PotentialExchange.h:158-171), so
                                 this minimal positive pair is used to
                                 disable the branch; the same values
                                 appear in the unit test
                                 Tests/ProcessLib/RichardsMechanics/
                                 DSMMicroMacroSingleIntegrationPoint.cpp:
                                 663. This is not a material parameter
                                 and is not attributed to a literature
                                 source. The physical literature value it
                                 substitutes for is A = 2.2e-20 J
                                 (Israelachvili and Adams 1978); that
                                 value does not apply to the placeholder
                                 used here.
    specific surface Sa        : 1.0 m2/kg, placeholder paired with A
                                 above (MX-80 is order 1e5 to 1e6 m2/kg).

  Reference VTU    : this output is a regression baseline for the
                     current constitutive formulation; it is not a
                     validated physical result. It reflects constitutive
                     corrections to the micro-macro potential-exchange
                     formulation, including a Maxwell-consistent
                     unification of the liquid chemical potential and a
                     sign/weighting correction to the swelling-stress
                     term (recast as (1-phi_M)*p_film).

  Known deviations from the standard DSM configuration:
    1. bishops_effective_stress uses BishopsPowerLaw(exponent=1) rather
       than BishopsSaturationCutoff(cutoff=1), which is the standard
       choice used elsewhere in the DSM benchmark set.
    2. The pressure convergence tolerance (abstol = 5e-8 Pa) is small
       relative to the suction scale of the problem (order 1e6 Pa), and
       no relative tolerances (reltols) are set.
    3. Across the beacon benchmark decks, the Hamaker-constant
       placeholder takes three different values (1e-30 / 6e-20 /
       5.1e-21 J); none matches the literature value used elsewhere in
       this benchmark set (2.2e-20 J).
    4. The unit of alpha_M (mass_exchange_coefficient) is not documented
       by OGS; no unit is asserted here.
-->
    <mesh axially_symmetric="true">beacon_1b_domain.vtu</mesh>
    <geometry>beacon_1b.gml</geometry>
    <processes>
        <process>
            <name>RM</name>
            <type>RICHARDS_MECHANICS</type>
            <integration_order>2</integration_order>
            <micro_porosity>
                <mass_exchange_coefficient>1e-13</mass_exchange_coefficient>
                <nonlinear_solver><maximum_iterations>100</maximum_iterations><residuum_tolerance>1e-8</residuum_tolerance><increment_tolerance>1e-20</increment_tolerance></nonlinear_solver>
            </micro_porosity>
            <potential_exchange>
                <enabled>true</enabled>
                <pressure_tolerance>0.0</pressure_tolerance>
                <hamaker_constant>1e-30</hamaker_constant>
                <specific_surface>1.0</specific_surface>
                <micro_solid_density_reference>2650</micro_solid_density_reference>
                <micro_solid_volume_fraction_reference>0.6</micro_solid_volume_fraction_reference>
                <initial_micro_water_content>0.1</initial_micro_water_content>
                <fd_jacobian_for_exchange>false</fd_jacobian_for_exchange>
                            <!-- Floors declared inert (0.0 = no floor); the parser
                     requires both keys to be declared together. Same
                     inert declaration as used in the MS33 "form (a)"
                     decks. -->
                <macro_porosity_floor>0.0</macro_porosity_floor>
                <micro_water_content_floor>0.0</micro_water_content_floor>
            </potential_exchange>
            <constitutive_relation><type>LinearElasticIsotropic</type><youngs_modulus>E</youngs_modulus><poissons_ratio>nu</poissons_ratio></constitutive_relation>
            <process_variables><pressure>pressure</pressure><displacement>displacement</displacement></process_variables>
            <secondary_variables>
                <secondary_variable name="sigma"/><secondary_variable name="swelling_stress"/><secondary_variable name="epsilon"/><secondary_variable name="velocity"/><secondary_variable name="saturation"/><secondary_variable name="porosity"/><secondary_variable name="transport_porosity"/><secondary_variable name="dry_density_solid"/><secondary_variable name="micro_saturation"/><secondary_variable name="micro_pressure"/>
            </secondary_variables>
            <specific_body_force>0 0</specific_body_force>
            <initial_stress>sigma0</initial_stress>
            <mass_lumping>true</mass_lumping>
        </process>
    </processes>
    <media>
        <medium id="0">
            <phases>
                <phase><type>AqueousLiquid</type><properties><property><name>viscosity</name><type>Constant</type><value>1e-3</value></property><property><name>density</name><type>Constant</type><value>1e3</value></property></properties></phase>
                <phase><type>Solid</type><properties><property><name>density</name><type>Constant</type><value>2780</value></property><property><name>swelling_stress_rate</name><type>SaturationDependentSwelling</type><swelling_pressures>1.1e7 1.1e7 1.1e7</swelling_pressures><exponents>1 1 1</exponents><lower_saturation_limit>0</lower_saturation_limit><upper_saturation_limit>1</upper_saturation_limit></property></properties></phase>
            </phases>
            <properties>
                <property><name>transport_porosity</name><type>TransportPorosityFromMassBalance</type><initial_porosity>phi_tr0</initial_porosity><minimal_porosity>0</minimal_porosity><maximal_porosity>1</maximal_porosity></property>
                <property><name>biot_coefficient</name><type>Constant</type><value>1.0</value></property>
                <property><name>permeability</name><type>Constant</type><value>5e-16</value></property>
                <property><name>porosity</name><type>PorosityFromMassBalance</type><initial_porosity>phi0</initial_porosity><minimal_porosity>0</minimal_porosity><maximal_porosity>1</maximal_porosity></property>
                <property><name>reference_temperature</name><type>Constant</type><value>293.15</value></property>
                <property><name>relative_permeability</name><type>Constant</type><value>1</value></property>
                <property><name>saturation</name><type>SaturationVanGenuchten</type><residual_liquid_saturation>0.0</residual_liquid_saturation><residual_gas_saturation>0</residual_gas_saturation><exponent>0.5</exponent><p_b>5e5</p_b></property>
                <property><name>saturation_micro</name><type>SaturationVanGenuchten</type><residual_liquid_saturation>0</residual_liquid_saturation><residual_gas_saturation>0</residual_gas_saturation><exponent>0.5</exponent><p_b>5e6</p_b></property>
                <property><name>bishops_effective_stress</name><type>BishopsPowerLaw</type><exponent>1</exponent></property>
            </properties>
        </medium>
    </media>
    <time_loop>
        <processes><process ref="RM"><nonlinear_solver>nonlinear_solver</nonlinear_solver><convergence_criterion><norm_type>NORM2</norm_type><type>PerComponentDeltaX</type><abstols>5e-8 1e-13 1e-13</abstols></convergence_criterion><time_discretization><type>BackwardEuler</type></time_discretization><time_stepping><type>FixedTimeStepping</type><t_initial>0.0</t_initial><t_end>1e3</t_end><timesteps><pair><repeat>20</repeat><delta_t>50</delta_t></pair></timesteps></time_stepping></process></processes>
        <output><type>VTK</type><prefix>beacon_1b_dsm_micromacro_smoke</prefix><suffix>_t_{:time}</suffix><fixed_output_times>1e3</fixed_output_times><variables><variable>pressure</variable><variable>displacement</variable><variable>saturation</variable><variable>micro_pressure</variable><variable>micro_saturation</variable><variable>swelling_stress</variable><variable>sigma</variable></variables></output>
    </time_loop>
    <parameters>
        <parameter><name>sigma0</name><type>Function</type><expression>0</expression><expression>0</expression><expression>0</expression><expression>0</expression></parameter>
        <parameter><name>E</name><type>Constant</type><value>40e6</value></parameter>
        <parameter><name>nu</name><type>Constant</type><value>0.2</value></parameter>
        <parameter><name>phi0</name><type>Constant</type><value>0.5</value></parameter>
        <parameter><name>phi_tr0</name><type>Constant</type><value>0.4</value></parameter>
        <parameter><name>displacement0</name><type>Constant</type><values>0 0</values></parameter>
        <parameter><name>pressure_ic</name><type>Constant</type><values>-1e6</values></parameter>
        <parameter><name>dirichlet0</name><type>Constant</type><value>0</value></parameter>
        <parameter><name>top_pressure</name><type>Constant</type><value>0</value></parameter>
        <parameter><name>bottom_pressure</name><type>Constant</type><value>1e4</value></parameter>
    </parameters>
    <process_variables>
        <process_variable><name>displacement</name><components>2</components><order>1</order><initial_condition>displacement0</initial_condition><boundary_conditions>
            <boundary_condition><geometrical_set>beacon_1b_geometry</geometrical_set><geometry>left</geometry><type>Dirichlet</type><component>0</component><parameter>dirichlet0</parameter></boundary_condition>
            <boundary_condition><geometrical_set>beacon_1b_geometry</geometrical_set><geometry>right</geometry><type>Dirichlet</type><component>0</component><parameter>dirichlet0</parameter></boundary_condition>
            <boundary_condition><geometrical_set>beacon_1b_geometry</geometrical_set><geometry>bottom</geometry><type>Dirichlet</type><component>1</component><parameter>dirichlet0</parameter></boundary_condition>
            <boundary_condition><geometrical_set>beacon_1b_geometry</geometrical_set><geometry>top</geometry><type>Dirichlet</type><component>1</component><parameter>dirichlet0</parameter></boundary_condition>
        </boundary_conditions></process_variable>
        <process_variable><name>pressure</name><components>1</components><order>1</order><initial_condition>pressure_ic</initial_condition><boundary_conditions>
            <boundary_condition><geometrical_set>beacon_1b_geometry</geometrical_set><geometry>top</geometry><type>Dirichlet</type><component>0</component><parameter>top_pressure</parameter></boundary_condition>
            <boundary_condition><geometrical_set>beacon_1b_geometry</geometrical_set><geometry>bottom</geometry><type>Dirichlet</type><component>0</component><parameter>bottom_pressure</parameter></boundary_condition>
        </boundary_conditions></process_variable>
    </process_variables>
    <nonlinear_solvers><nonlinear_solver><name>nonlinear_solver</name><type>Newton</type><max_iter>30</max_iter><linear_solver>general_linear_solver</linear_solver></nonlinear_solver></nonlinear_solvers>
    <linear_solvers><linear_solver><name>general_linear_solver</name><eigen><solver_type>SparseLU</solver_type><scaling>true</scaling></eigen></linear_solver></linear_solvers>
</OpenGeoSysProject>
